    <title>
        feat: generate the full-weight torus by root subgroups (#28975)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240895760?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>sqrt-of-2</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/sqrt-of-2</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: generate the full-weight torus by root subgroups (#28975)

This PR proves that the full-weight admissible lattice&amp;#39;s weight torus lies in the subgroup generated by its numbered positive and negative simple-root subgroups, over every commutative ring. Identify the integral toral and root-generated defining Hopf ideals and group schemes, prove the canonical inclusion is an isomorphism, and deduce transported ideal equality and root-only rigidity.

Advance `ChevalleyGroups/README.md`, milestone C2, “Chevalley data, their group schemes, and root data”, specifically “Generation of the torus (simply connected)”. The designated consumer milestone is `CFSGStatement/README.md`, Layer 1, §1.1 “Canonical points and pinning”: the generation and homomorphism-determination requirements for `Gᶜ_d` consume ChevalleyGroups C2&amp;#39;s torus generation together with C4&amp;#39;s point-generation theorem. Dependency edge: CFSGStatement §1.1 → ChevalleyGroups C2/C4 → root generation of the full-weight realization&amp;#39;s torus. After this PR, the canonical constructor/realization identification and certification, the remaining all-root scheme interface, and C4&amp;#39;s specialization and point-generation theorem remain before §1.1 can be completed; integral scheme generation here does not claim generation of all specialized points.

Choose this missing generation result because the full-weight module, faithfulness, lattice and weight basis are already on main. The open full-weight datum (#28667), all-root point maps (#28340), torus-restriction comparison (#28723), and diagram scheme action (#28726) supply different interfaces; this PR imports none of their content. No second canonical carrier or conditional replacement for a missing constructor is introduced.

Add `TauCeti/Algebra/AlgebraicGroup/Chevalley/Generation.lean` (162 lines). Reuse the generic Kostant coroot theorem, `IsSl2Triple.map`, and the universal-torus generation criterion. Follow the existing E7 minuscule generation proof pattern, credited in the module along with Steinberg, Chapter 3, and Carter, §§6.4 and 7.1. No Mathlib infrastructure or external formalization is vendored.

Read the shared protocol and all ten rubrics: scope, correctness, reuse, attribution, api-design, generality, placement, naming, documentation and proof-quality. Self-review makes the representation-specific sl₂ step private, retains arbitrary-ring and arbitrary-valid-type generality, and preserves the distinction between transported integral ideals and generation anew after non-flat specialization. Repeated pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti searches find no existing full-weight specialization replacing these results.

Local verification passes `lake exe cache get`, plain whole-library `lake build --iofail` (67,514 jobs), the changed-module axiom audit, all fourteen changed-module environment linters, and whitespace checking. These are local checks, not CI; CI verifies the pushed head, including transitive axioms and global checks.

Local changed-file checks: `scope: scoped against e16f84d439640b7f18e006301f34a1566b5b0151`.

`local-axioms: checked 1 changed module(s), 29 declaration(s); 0 violation(s). Transitive axiom and global ownership checks run in CI.`

Roadmap: ChevalleyGroups
Consumer roadmap: CFSGStatement

