    <title>
        feat: critical points and Morse criterion for the projective moment f…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/339378563?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>tauceti-ai-for-science</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-ai-for-science</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: critical points and Morse criterion for the projective moment function (#29473)

This PR extends the moment function `TauCeti.projectiveMomentFunction 𝕜 w` on `ℙ 𝕜 (Fin (n + 1) → 𝕜)` (from https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/pull/27901 &amp;quot;feat: the moment function on projective space is a Morse function&amp;quot;) with the results for arbitrary weights and the real count. Over `𝕜 = ℝ`, with values `[v] ↦ (∑ j, w j * v j ^ 2) / ∑ j, v j ^ 2`, it is the weighted Rayleigh quotient on `ℝℙⁿ`.

All new declarations are in `TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Morse/Projectivization.lean`:
- `mk_mem_criticalPoints_projectiveMomentFunction_iff`: for arbitrary weights, `[v]` is critical exactly when every nonzero coordinate `v j` carries the weight `w j` equal to the value at `[v]`, i.e. the critical points are the eigenlines of the diagonal form.
- `isManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint_projectiveMomentFunction_iff`: `[eₖ]` is nondegenerate exactly when `w k` is a simple weight.
- `isMorse_projectiveMomentFunction_iff`: the function is Morse exactly when the weights are pairwise distinct.
- `criticalCount_projectiveMomentFunction_real`: on `ℝℙⁿ` with distinct weights there is exactly one critical point of each index `j ≤ n`, and none of larger index.
- `projectiveMomentFunction_mk_single`: the value at `[eₖ]` is `w k`.

In the chart model, `ProjectiveMomentChart.fderiv_model_eq_zero_iff_forall` describes all critical points of the model, with its value at such a point given by `ProjectiveMomentChart.model_eq_of_forall`. The existing `fderiv_model_eq_zero_iff` is now its corollary. `ProjectiveMomentChart.isNondegenerateCriticalPoint_model_zero_iff` adds the converse of nondegeneracy at the origin. The counting step uses `Set.injective_ncard_setOf_lt` in `TauCeti/Data/Set/Card.lean`: for an injective map into a linear order, the number of values below `f a` determines `a`. With `Set.encard_setOf_ncard_setOf_lt_eq` there, each `j &amp;lt; Nat.card ι` is the rank of exactly one index.

Roadmap: MorseTheory

The target is the RP² acceptance test of MorseTheory milestone M4, &amp;quot;Strong inequalities and topology tests&amp;quot;: &amp;quot;For RP² … use the quadratic coordinate function with three distinct weights: three critical points and no perfect Morse function over ℚ, contrasted with its perfect F₂ count&amp;quot;. The same function `f[x:y:z]=(y²+2z²)/(x²+y²+z²)` is the RP² acceptance test of M2&amp;#39;s change-of-chart comparison. For `n = 2` and `w = ![0, 1, 2]`, `criticalCount_projectiveMomentFunction_real` gives one critical point each of index 0, 1 and 2, which is the &amp;quot;three critical points&amp;quot; clause stated directly as counts by index. `isMorse_projectiveMomentFunction_iff` shows that distinct weights are exactly what the test needs. The carrier is the smooth projectivization `ℙ ℝ (Fin (n + 1) → ℝ)`, which is homeomorphic to the CW carrier `RealProjectiveSpace n` through `RealProjectiveSpace.homeomorphProjectivization`. What remains for the M4 test after this PR is to compare these counts with the Betti numbers of RP² over ℚ (1, 0, 0) and over F₂ (1, 1, 1) through the Morse inequalities.

&amp;lt;!--tauceti-target:v1 {&amp;quot;focus&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MorseTheory&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;id&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;projective-rayleigh-quotient-morse-function&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

