    <title>
        refactor(Analysis/Normed/Module/StrictGenerators): drop the redundant…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298123923?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>tauceti-redteam</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-redteam</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(Analysis/Normed/Module/StrictGenerators): drop the redundant NormOneClass hypothesis (#30855)

Roadmap: RestrictedPowerSeries
&amp;lt;!--redteam:v1 {&amp;quot;owner&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;AI-DOOM-b743906b-281a-4ba5-939c-d5913cc9d39b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;findings&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;RT-20261106-370e29&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;patterns&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;redundant-hypothesis&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;severity&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MINOR&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

## What was wrong
`Submodule.exists_finset_norm_eq_one_of_exists_finset_eq_sum_smul` carried `[NormOneClass A]` as a section variable (Raised by Haiku survey h716-haiku). It was used only at `norm_one` for a nonzero generator `x`. Such an `x` forces `A` to be nontrivial, and Mathlib&amp;#39;s `NormMulClass.toNormOneClass` then gives `NormOneClass A` from `NormMulClass A`. The statement is the intended one (checked against its docstring and the module docstring: multiplicative ultrametric norm; roadmap `RestrictedPowerSeries` §5.3, normalised generators), and the excluded case (a trivial ring) has no nonzero generators, so it is not a junk value.

## The fix
Remove `[NormOneClass A]` from the section variable and derive it at the one use from nontriviality. No caller changes: the three Tate algebra importers (`FiniteModuleTopology`, `Groebner`, `Submodule`) build unchanged. The companion lead (dropping `[IsBoundedSMul A M]` from `isModuleTopology_of_exists_finset_eq_sum_smul` and the completeness theorems) is refuted: `IsModuleTopology A N` needs `ContinuousSMul A N`, which comes from `IsBoundedSMul`. Built `TauCeti.Analysis.Normed.Module.StrictGenerators` and its three direct importers, no messages; `scripts/lint-style.sh` clean.

Open PRs touching the file: none (cache refreshed 2026-11-06).

