      <name>tauceti-redteam</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-redteam</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(Analysis/Distribution/Mass/PolarDensity): split exists_le_one into a helper (#29734)

Roadmap: GeometricCurrents
&amp;lt;!--redteam:v1 {&amp;quot;owner&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;AI-DOOM-b743906b-281a-4ba5-939c-d5913cc9d39b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;findings&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;RT-20261106-9849f7&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;patterns&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;long-proof&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;severity&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MAJOR&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

## What was wrong
The private `exists_le_one` in `TauCeti/Analysis/Distribution/Mass/PolarDensity.lean` had a 68-code-line proof (the survey note said 80; measured). It assembles a measurable dual-valued density `g` of `T` against a dominating measure and then normalises it by the density of `‖T‖`.

## Evidence
`git show origin/main:TauCeti/Analysis/Distribution/Mass/PolarDensity.lean | awk &amp;#39;NR&amp;gt;=89&amp;amp;&amp;amp;NR&amp;lt;=164&amp;#39; | grep -v &amp;#39;^\s*$&amp;#39; | grep -cv &amp;#39;^\s*--&amp;#39;` gives 68 (origin/main afa08a3ed1).

## The fix
Private helper `exists_measurable_dual_density` (41 code lines, docstring) takes the assembly of `ρ`, `g`, local integrability and the representation `T φ = ∫ g (φ x) ∂ρ`; the proof is the moved original block. `exists_le_one` keeps its statement byte for byte and is now 30 code lines. No other declaration changed, and nothing in the library imports this module. This does not use the general normalisation lemma of open #29708, which is not on main (no stacking); that PR concerns the same-shaped declaration in `BoundedVariation/PolarDecomposition`.

Built `TauCeti.Analysis.Distribution.Mass.PolarDensity`; `scripts/lint-style.sh` clean. Open PRs touching this file: #26591 and #28796; `git merge-tree --write-tree` of this head with each merges cleanly.

