    <title>
        refactor(FieldTheory/PurelyInseparable/Exponent): rescale an arbitrar…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6145801?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>harahu</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/harahu</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(FieldTheory/PurelyInseparable/Exponent): rescale an arbitrary basis (#29729)

Review pass over `TauCeti/FieldTheory/PurelyInseparable/Exponent.lean`. This PR refactors existing code and adds no new mathematics.

**Generality and correctness of the docstring:** `exists_basis_iterateFrobenius_eq_algebraMap` becomes `exists_iterateFrobenius_unitsSMul_eq_algebraMap`.
- Before, it produced *some* `Fin m`-indexed basis. Now it takes any basis `b : Module.Basis ι K L` and returns units `w : ι → Kˣ` and preimages `g : ι → A` with `iterateFrobenius K L p hn (b.unitsSMul w j) = algebraMap A K (g j)`. The module docstring already claimed that rescaling *any* basis works, but the old statement did not deliver that. Now it does.
- `[FiniteDimensional K L]` is dropped. Only `HasExponent K L` is used, so the lemma now also covers infinite-dimensional extensions that have an exponent.
- `[IsDomain A]` is dropped. It is implied by `IsFractionRing A K` with `K` a field, and the new proof does not need it.
- The equation is oriented `iterateFrobenius … = algebraMap …` so that it matches the name. The name changes because the conclusion no longer existentially quantifies a basis.

**Proof quality:**
- The basis lemma now uses `IsLocalization.surj` and `IsLocalization.map_units` to clear denominators, instead of `div_surjective`, a nonzero-denominator side lemma and `field_simp`.
- `pow_mem_of_finrank_le_pow` now handles both characteristic cases with a single `elemExponent K a ≤ n` bound followed by `pow_mem`. The ad hoc witness is gone.
- `exponent_le_of_finrank_le_pow` is now a term-mode proof.

**Callers updated:** `TauCeti/RingTheory/IntegralClosure/PurelyInseparable.lean` (`IsIntegralClosure.finite_mvPolynomial_of_isPurelyInseparable`) now applies the lemma to `Module.finBasis K M` and uses the rescaled basis.

Built: the edited modules, plus every module that references the changed names or directly imports the file (`FieldTheory.Separable.PrimeDegree`, `AlgebraicGeometry.EllipticCurve.Isogeny.RelativeFrobenius.Factorisation`).

Roadmap: SchemeAndStackFoundations

