    <title>
        feat: deck transformations shift primitives on period covers by perio…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/339378563?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>tauceti-ai-for-science</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-ai-for-science</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: deck transformations shift primitives on period covers by periods (#29439)

This PR proves that a primitive of a pulled-back closed one-form on a subgroup cover is shifted by periods under deck transformations. On the period-kernel cover this is the equivariance `f̃(h·y) = f̃(y) + P(h)`.

Roadmap target: `MorseNovikov/README.md`, milestone N2, §2.2 &amp;quot;Periods and connected abelian covers&amp;quot;. It proves the API item &amp;quot;A primitive upstairs obeys f̃(h·x)=f̃(x)+P(h)&amp;quot;, as part of &amp;quot;Build the lifted smooth structure, metric/vector field and primitive, with deck-equivariance&amp;quot;. The period-kernel cover, its lifted atlas, its deck group identified with the period image (`PeriodCover.deckEquiv`) and the existence of a primitive (`PeriodCover.exists_primitive`) are already on `main`. The equivariance of that primitive was missing. §2.4 consumes it, where the potential of the lifted critical points obeys `F(hs) = F(s) − N(h)` with `N = −P`.

Contents:
- `TauCeti.UniversalCover.SubgroupQuotient.apply_mk_eq_apply_basepoint_add_pathClassIntegral`: on the cover attached to any subgroup `K ≤ π₁(M, x)`, a `C²` primitive `f` of the pullback of a closed `C¹` form `θ` satisfies `f [e] = f (basepoint) + ∫_e θ` for every path class `e` from the basepoint. The proof integrates `df` along the lift of `e` built from its initial segments, using the existing fundamental theorem of calculus for path classes and naturality of path-class integrals under pullback. No hypothesis `K ≤ ker P` is needed, since a primitive can only exist under that condition. The coefficients may be any complete normed space.
- `TauCeti.UniversalCover.apply_deckSubgroupQuotientProjEquivOfNormal_mk_apply`: for normal `K` over a path-connected base, the deck transformation given by the class of a loop `g` changes `f` by `−periodHom θ x g`. The sign is forced by the existing convention that this deck transformation prepends `g⁻¹`.
- `TauCeti.PeriodCover.apply_deck_apply`: on the period-kernel cover, `f (d y) = f y + P d` for every deck transformation `d`, where `P d` is the period labelling `d` under `deckEquiv`. This is the roadmap&amp;#39;s `f̃(h·x) = f̃(x) + P(h)`. In particular, when all periods vanish, every primitive is deck-invariant (the roadmap check for exact forms).
- `TauCeti.pathClassIntegral_cast` (in `Period.lean`, `@[simp]`): casting the endpoints of a path class does not change its integral. The proofs above need it to identify the projected lift with the original path class without relying on unexposed definitional unfolding.

Files: `TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/DeRham/Cover.lean` (+98, including the module docstring update) and `TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/DeRham/Period.lean` (+7). No Mathlib material is vendored. The mathematics follows M. Farber, *Topology of Closed One-Forms*, §1.1, and A. Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, §1.3, both already cited in `Cover.lean`.

After this PR, §2.2 still needs the `H₁(X̃) → H₁(X) → H → 0` exactness statement and the positive/negative flow comparison of the lifted vector field. The second waits on the metric-dual trajectory construction in open #29044.

Local checks: `lake build` of the changed modules and their dependents succeeds. The whole-library build fails only in `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.EllipticCurve.MinimalModel.Valuation` (and modules downstream of it), and it fails identically on unmodified `main` (`b638273ca4`). That breakage also blocks the whole-library `lake exe axioms` and `lake exe module-system` locally. I checked the four new declarations with `#print axioms` instead (only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`). `scripts/lint-env.sh` could not run because `uvx` is unavailable here. Running the Batteries/Mathlib `#lint` on both changed modules found 0 errors with 15 linters, including `simpNF`. CI verifies the pushed head.

Roadmap: MorseNovikov

