    <author>
      <name>tauceti-ai-for-science</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-ai-for-science</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: the skein mapping cone of the unnormalized Khovanov complex (#28429)

This PR adds the skein mapping cone of the unnormalized Khovanov complex at an arbitrary crossing. For a planar code `D` with a crossing `c` and resolutions `D_A = D.resolveCrossing c true`, `D_B = D.resolveCrossing c false`, it constructs the saddle map of cubes `resolveCrossingSaddle : ⟦D_A⟧ʲ ⟶ ⟦D_B⟧ʲ⁻¹` (shown to act on circle tensors as the merge or split `resolutionEdgeMap` of `D` at `c`), the identification `khovanovBracketMappingConeIso : mappingCone (saddle) ≅ ⟦D⟧ʲ⟦1⟧` with its vertex formulas (no sign on the `A`-face, sign `-(-1)^#{a ∈ S | a.castSucc &amp;lt; c}` on the `B`-face), and the skein triangle `⟦D_A⟧ʲ ⟶ ⟦D_B⟧ʲ⁻¹ ⟶ ⟦D⟧ʲ⟦1⟧ ⟶ ⟦D_A⟧ʲ⟦1⟧` with `khovanovBracketSkeinTriangle_distinguished` in the homotopy category.

The general cube input lives in `Algebra/Homology/Cube/MappingCone.lean`: for a cube `F : Finset (Fin (n + 1)) ⥤ C` and any index `c`, the faces `cubeFaceZeroAt`, `cubeFaceOneAt`, the face map `cubeFaceMapAt`, and `cubeComplexMappingConeIsoAt`, obtained by moving `c` to the front with the existing reordering isomorphism `cubeComplexReindexIso` and then applying the existing `WithBot` mapping-cone decomposition `cubeComplexMappingConeIso`. It is characterised on vertices in both directions. `ResolveCrossing.lean` gains the one-line inclusion `resolveCrossingVertex_true_subset_false`.

Roadmap target: `KhovanovHomology/README.md`, section K5 (Exact sequences, coefficients, symmetry, and based links), first paragraph: &amp;quot;For a selected crossing, put it first in the crossing order and decompose its cube into the 0 and 1 faces. Prove the unnormalized short exact sequence with 1-face term `C̄(D₁)⟨1⟩[-1]`, middle `C̄(D)`, and quotient `C̄(D₀)` ... Construct the saddle map and the cone comparison with its sign on the 1-face summand. Export the resulting long exact sequence&amp;quot;. This PR supplies the saddle map, the cone comparison with its 1-face sign (including the reordering sign when `c` is not first), and the distinguished triangle; rotated, it is the degreewise split sequence `⟦D_B⟧ʲ⁻¹⟦-1⟧ ⟶ ⟦D⟧ʲ ⟶ ⟦D_A⟧ʲ`, whose `B`-term is `C̄(D₁)⟨1⟩[-1]`. It builds on the face identification `resolveCrossingCubeIso` and the `WithBot` cone decomposition already on main. What remains of this K5 item after this PR is exporting the explicit homology long exact sequence from the distinguished triangle and translating it to the normalized complexes with the `n₊, n₋` shifts and orientation choices of the three diagrams.

Roadmap: KhovanovHomology

&amp;lt;!--tauceti-target:v1 {&amp;quot;focus&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;KhovanovHomology&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;id&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;khovanov-skein-exact-sequence&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

References: M. Khovanov, A categorification of the Jones polynomial, Duke Math. J. 101 (2000), §3.4; D. Bar-Natan, On Khovanov&amp;#39;s categorification of the Jones polynomial, Algebr. Geom. Topol. 2 (2002), §3.1. No Mathlib material is vendored; the triangle uses Mathlib&amp;#39;s `HomotopyCategory.mappingCone_triangleh_distinguished`.

🤖 Prepared with Claude Code

