  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/6b8e66e396460a0a9987d158bb801b0d846a9863</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/commit/6b8e66e396460a0a9987d158bb801b0d846a9863"/>
    <title>
        refactor(RingTheory/AdjoinRoot/Basic): drop the hypothesis i ≤ n from…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298123923?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>tauceti-redteam</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-redteam</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(RingTheory/AdjoinRoot/Basic): drop the hypothesis i ≤ n from the annihilator lemmas of x ^ i in R[X]/(X ^ n) (#29613)

Roadmap: StablePeriodicCurved
&amp;lt;!--redteam:v1 {&amp;quot;owner&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;AI-DOOM-b743906b-281a-4ba5-939c-d5913cc9d39b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;findings&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;RT-20261105-cef233&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;patterns&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;needless-hypothesis&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;severity&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MAJOR&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

## What was wrong

- **RT-20261105-cef233** (MAJOR, suspected): the hypothesis `hi : i ≤ n` of `AdjoinRoot.root_X_pow_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff` (`x ^ i * c = 0 ↔ x ^ (n - i) ∣ c` in `R[X]/(X ^ n)`, `x` the class of `X`) and of its companion `root_X_pow_sub_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff` is redundant: for `i &amp;gt; n` one has `x ^ i = 0` (as `X ^ n ∣ X ^ i`) and `n - i = 0` in `ℕ`, so the first reads `0 = 0 ↔ 1 ∣ c` and the second `c = 0 ↔ 0 ∣ c`, both true. Mathematically `ann(x ^ i) = ann(0) = A = (x ^ 0)`, so the `hi`-free statement is the correct general one with `n - i` read as `max (n - i) 0`. The hypothesis was carried needlessly by public consumers in four files, where it fed only these two lemmas: `cyclicModuleRootPowProjectiveResolution` and its five companions (`ModuleCat/Projective/CyclicResolution.lean`), `stableModuleLoopCyclicModuleRootPowIso` and `stableModuleLoopLoopCyclicModuleRootPowIso` (`FGModuleCat/Stable/Syzygy.lean`), `finrank_map_ker_smul_op_root_pow` (`FGModuleCat/Cyclic.lean`) and, through it, `finrank_stableModuleHom_cyclicModule_root_pow` (`FGModuleCat/Stable/CyclicHom.lean`).

## Evidence

The hunt&amp;#39;s probe (`/tmp/q1351/hunt-adjoinroot`) proves both lemmas without `hi` by a four-line case split and rebuilds the four consumer declarations from the `hi`-free versions; this PR is that change, in place. Per the removable-hypothesis rule the statements were checked first: (a) the docstrings state the annihilator identity &amp;quot;for `i ≤ n`&amp;quot; only because the proof needed it, and the identity is the intended one; (b) the roadmap `StablePeriodicCurved` names the three consumer defs and `finrank_stableModuleHom` with their present conclusions (`Ω M_i ≅ M_{n-i}`, `Ω² M_i ≅ M_i`, the dimension formula), which keep their meaning (for `i &amp;gt; n`, `M_i = A` is free, so `Ω M_i ≅ 0 = M_0` and the stable Hom dimension `0` are the right values); (c) the literature statement (annihilators in a truncated polynomial ring) has no rank restriction; (d) the review site has no standard review of these declarations. So the hypothesis is genuinely unused, not a symptom of a misstatement. Decided by the Fable definition agent because three `def`s change their binders. Astra review is pending.

## The fix

- `root_X_pow_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff` and `root_X_pow_sub_pow_mul_eq_zero_iff` lose `hi`; each proof does `rcases le_or_gt i n`, keeps the original argument in the first case, and in the second rewrites `x ^ i = 0` and `n - i = 0` and closes by `simp`. Docstrings say what happens for `i &amp;gt; n`.
- `CyclicResolution.lean`: `cyclicModuleRootPowProjectiveResolution`, `…_complex`, `…XIso`, `…_π_f_zero`, `…_complex_d`, `…_complex_d_apply` and `range_…_complex_d_le` lose `hi`; since `hi` was what pinned `n` and `i`, the section now takes `(n i : ℕ)` explicitly, so the resolution is `cyclicModuleRootPowProjectiveResolution R n i`.
- `Syzygy.lean`: the two isomorphisms lose `hi` and take `n i` explicitly (`variable (n i) in`).
- `Cyclic.lean`: `finrank_map_ker_smul_op_root_pow` keeps only `hj : j ≤ n`. `CyclicHom.lean`: `finrank_stableModuleHom_cyclicModule_root_pow` loses `hj` as well (after review): for `j &amp;gt; n` the target `M_j` is free, `x ^ j = x ^ min j n = 0`, so the proof reduces to the case `j&amp;#39; = min j n ≤ n` and the formula still reads `min (min i j) (min (n - i) (n - j))` (`0`); the module docstring is updated.
- `MatrixFactorization/Polynomial/Periodic.lean`: the private `range_rootPowHom_sub_eq_ker` loses `hi` (its two callers adjust); `powerXPeriodicComplex` keeps `hi`, which it uses for its own reasons.

No declaration is renamed or deleted; no statement is weakened.

**Checks:** built `TauCeti.RingTheory.AdjoinRoot.Basic`, `TauCeti.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Projective.CyclicResolution`, `TauCeti.Algebra.Category.FGModuleCat.Stable.Syzygy`, `TauCeti.Algebra.Category.FGModuleCat.Cyclic`, `TauCeti.Algebra.Category.FGModuleCat.Stable.CyclicHom` and `TauCeti.CommutativeAlgebra.MatrixFactorization.Polynomial.Periodic` (every module that mentions a changed name) with zero errors and zero warnings (`CyclicHom` re-built after the review fix); `scripts/lint-style.sh` clean. Open PRs touching these files (open-PR file cache of 2026-11-06T06:17:55Z, 1719 open PRs): none.

## Why the changed definition is still the standard one

`cyclicModuleRootPowProjectiveResolution R n i` is the same two-periodic free resolution `⋯ → A --x^(n-i)--&amp;gt; A --x^i--&amp;gt; A → M_i` of `M_i = A/(x^i)` over `A = R[X]/(X^n)` as before, now for every `i`; for `i &amp;gt; n` it is the (exact) resolution of the free module `A` by `⋯ → A --0--&amp;gt; A --1--&amp;gt; A → A`. The syzygy isomorphisms are likewise unchanged on `i ≤ n`. Astra review is pending.

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

Co-authored-by: Chris Birkbeck &amp;lt;c.birkbeck@uea.ac.uk&amp;gt;
Source-PR: TauCetiProject/TauCeti#29613
Accepted-Head: 80fe4bd3b6cc5cd46863534c48c8ba21d27a8cde&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/62b35b1862f5d2301ead264191eef7223d518f97</id>
