    <title>
        feat: identify torsion in the module of compatible pairs (#29726)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240895760?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>sqrt-of-2</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/sqrt-of-2</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: identify torsion in the module of compatible pairs (#29726)

This PR identifies the ideal-power torsion of the module of compatible pairs with that of its prescribed formal-neighbourhood factor. Prove bijectivity of the canonical projection on primary components when the complementary factor has no torsion and the overlap map kills torsion; impose no finite-generation, Noetherian or flatness hypotheses.

Advance LocalPurity/README.md §1.3, “Completion and restriction to a hypersurface”, milestone `finite_extend_of_completion` (Stacks 0BLH), through its prescribed compatible-pairs construction in Proposition 15.91.16 (05ER). The immediate consumer is the injectivity proof for the scalar-extension comparison from that kernel module: its torsion restriction must be injective, since the complementary sections have no ideal-power torsion. This PR establishes the stronger, canonical bijection on torsion, rather than assuming that torsion comparison as part of a gluing structure. After this PR, the completion-extension milestone still needs the full scalar-extension comparison and extension-reconstruction assembly, algebraization and finite-morphism assembly.

The explicit dependency chain is LocalPurity §1.3 `finite_extend_of_completion` / `extends_iff_completion_extends` → §1.4 `finiteEtale_extend_of_hypersurface` → §2.1 `Algebra.etale_of_finiteNormal_of_isRegularLocalRing` → the designated consumer PurityOfBranchLocus/README.md §2.1 `Scheme.Hom.exists_etale_of_formallyUnramified_stalk_codimOne` (0BMB). Choose this missing construction input because the branch-purity foundations are already on main, while unrestricted local purity remains incomplete. The open injectivity criterion (#29633) takes torsion injectivity as an input; this PR computes that input for the actual kernel construction. The localization comparison (#29654) and torsion-cokernel computation (#29669) concern different maps. Import no unmerged work.

Add `TauCeti/Algebra/Module/Torsion/Pullback.lean` (68 lines), exporting one theorem and no new definitions, predicates, instances or notation. Keep this general module result in the existing torsion directory and the `Ideal` namespace. Reuse Mathlib&amp;#39;s `Ideal.primaryComponent.map`, `primaryComponent_map_mem` and product linear maps, and Tau Ceti&amp;#39;s `primaryComponent_comap_subtype`. Cite Stacks 05ER in the module; no Mathlib infrastructure or external formalization is vendored.

Read the shared protocol and all ten rubrics: scope, correctness, reuse, attribution, api-design, generality, placement, naming, documentation and proof-quality. Self-review finds no duplicate comparison or missing characteristic API. Remove an unused local map and avoid requiring the whole overlap to be torsion-free: only its map from the prescribed module must kill torsion. Retain additive-monoid generality for the two factors. An importing-only client checks the nonzero torsion example with ideal `(2)` over `ℤ`, factors `ℤ` and `ℤ/4ℤ`, and overlap `ℤ`; it also constructs the linear equivalence when the second map is zero without a torsion-free overlap assumption.

Local verification passes Mathlib cache retrieval, plain whole-library `lake build --iofail` (67,628 jobs), the importing client, whitespace checking, the changed-module axiom audit and all fourteen changed-module environment linters. The post-commit scope selects the same single module, with unchanged source. These are local checks, not CI; CI verifies the pushed head, including transitive axioms and global ownership checks.

Local changed-file checks:

`scope: scoped against afa08a3ed16fb167e35de371afb1eb03fbc5913a`

`local-axioms: checked 1 changed module(s), 3 declaration(s); 0 violation(s). Transitive axiom and global ownership checks run in CI.`

Roadmap: LocalPurity
Consumer roadmap: PurityOfBranchLocus

&amp;lt;!--tauceti-target:v1 {&amp;quot;focus&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;LocalPurity&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;id&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;primarycomponent-map-snd-ker-coprod-bijective&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

