    <title>
        refactor(Algebra/Lie/NormTwoShell/Basic): split the three-distinct-ro…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298123923?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>tauceti-redteam</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-redteam</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(Algebra/Lie/NormTwoShell/Basic): split the three-distinct-roots Jacobi proof below 50 lines (#29541)

Roadmap: ReductiveGroups
&amp;lt;!--redteam:v1 {&amp;quot;owner&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;AI-DOOM-b743906b-281a-4ba5-939c-d5913cc9d39b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;findings&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;RT-20261106-s155c&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;patterns&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;long-proof&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;severity&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MAJOR&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

## What was wrong
The private theorem `Matrix.ShellLieAlgebra.jacobi_root_root_root_of_ne` in `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/NormTwoShell/Basic.lean` had a 73-code-line proof on main 72cbdfb14e. Raised by Haiku survey h146-haiku; the count is measured.

## Evidence
`awk &amp;#39;NR&amp;gt;=498&amp;amp;&amp;amp;NR&amp;lt;=574&amp;#39; &amp;lt;file&amp;gt; | grep -v &amp;#39;^\s*$&amp;#39; | grep -cv &amp;#39;^\s*--&amp;#39;` gave 73. After the change the proof has 49 code lines (50 with the `:= by` line) and the new helper about 20.

## The fix
One private helper with a docstring, `jacobi_terms_of_add_add_eq_zero` (the case where all three pairings are `-1`), replaces an inline `have` block. The sign-parity rewrites use the existing `TauCeti.negOnePow_mul_negOnePow_of_even` with `Int.negOnePow_add` and `Int.negOnePow_succ` (no private sign lemmas), and the pairing bounds come directly from `Matrix.PosDef.neg_one_le_dotProduct_mulVec` and `Matrix.PosDef.dotProduct_mulVec_le_one` (no conjunction wrapper). The norm of `a + b + c` is the new public lemma `Matrix.IsSymm.dotProduct_mulVec_add_add_of_mem_normTwoShell` in `TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/NormTwoShell/Basic.lean`, listed in that module&amp;#39;s docstring. The Jacobi statement is byte-identical and no existing declaration changed. The two modules and the five direct importers of the Lie module (`Cartan`, `CoverLift`, `FullCartan.Basic`, `Killing`, `Serre`) build clean; `lint-style.sh` clean.

## Overlapping open PRs
Open PRs #26591 (removal of unused tactic bindings across the library) and #26774 (integral folded Cartan lattice index) also touch this file; `git merge-tree` test merges of this head with each are clean, so they can land in any order.

