    <author>
      <name>tauceti-redteam</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-redteam</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(RepresentationTheory/Quiver/Preprojective/Koszul/Superadditive): extract the weighted Koszul recursion from the superadditive vanishing proof (#29499)

Roadmap: ZigzagPreprojective
&amp;lt;!--redteam:v1 {&amp;quot;owner&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;AI-DOOM-b743906b-281a-4ba5-939c-d5913cc9d39b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;findings&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;RT-20261106-s138b&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;patterns&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;long-proof&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;severity&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MAJOR&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

## What was wrong
`TauCeti.eq_zero_of_mem_preprojectiveCorner_of_two_mul_le_sum` (private) has a proof of 58 code lines, over the 50-line bar. Raised by Haiku survey H119-haiku and measured here.

## Evidence
`awk &amp;#39;NR&amp;gt;=342&amp;amp;&amp;amp;NR&amp;lt;=404&amp;#39; TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Quiver/Preprojective/Koszul/Superadditive.lean | grep -v &amp;#39;^\s*$&amp;#39; | grep -cv &amp;#39;^\s*--&amp;#39;` gives 58 on main c42b65f9ff. After the split the main proof has 35 code lines; the helper was 20 as first measured and is now shorter (see below).

## The fix
The Koszul recursion `2 * s (j + 1) ≤ s (j + 2) + s j` for weighted dimensions becomes the private documented lemma `two_mul_weighted_finrank_le_add`, taking the layer-dimension identity as hypothesis; the main proof supplies that identity from the injectivity induction hypothesis. The weighting and sum-transposition step it needs is the one already inside `add_one_mul_sum_mul_le_sum_mul` in `Algebra/Order/BigOperators/WeightedGrowth.lean`, so it is extracted there as the public lemma `two_mul_sum_mul_le_sum_mul_sum_mul`; that theorem&amp;#39;s local `key` and the helper both use it, and the helper only converts the vertex sums with `card_symmetrify_hom` and `hv`. Statements of existing declarations are byte-identical. Built: `TauCeti.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.WeightedGrowth`, `TauCeti.RepresentationTheory.Quiver.Preprojective.Koszul.Superadditive` and the importers `PathAlgebra.GolodShafarevich`, `HilbertSeries.ZigzagCartan` and `Koszul.NonDynkin`, no errors or warnings; `scripts/lint-style.sh` clean. No open PR touches these files.

