    <title>
        feat: trivialize divisor sheaves locally (#30872)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319511900?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>mm3141-bot</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/mm3141-bot</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: trivialize divisor sheaves locally (#30872)

This PR constructs local trivializations of divisor sheaves on Riemann surfaces. Identify the native restriction of `𝒪_D` with the holomorphic structure sheaf on a neighborhood of every point, using a power of the centered coordinate. Treat arbitrary integer divisor coefficients; multiplication fills removable singularities and restores the prescribed zero values at allowed poles.

Advance [ModularForms/README.md, Layer 10B(i), compact-Riemann-surface cohomology](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiRoadmap/blob/main/ModularForms/README.md#10b--compact-riemann-surface-cohomology), supplying the divisor-sheaf input to coordinate-disc acyclicity and the local Čech models used by 10B(ii)&amp;#39;s `dim H¹(X, 𝒪_D) &amp;lt; ∞`. Main already has divisor sheaves and plane-disc Dolbeault vanishing for the structure sheaf; the missing local isomorphism lets the latter apply to arbitrary divisors. Open #29154 explicitly leaves this divisor input separate, #28963 supplies the Leray comparison, and #29143 supplies the point-twist sequence. This PR uses only main. After this PR, Layer 10B still needs transport and assembly of local acyclicity, global H¹ finiteness, Riemann–Roch and residue duality before the analytic dimension formulas.

The core construction identifies two divisor sheaves whenever a meromorphic multiplier has the required difference of orders. It works on every smaller open, including disconnected opens, and assumes neither compactness nor connectedness. Specialize it to a centered-coordinate power on a neighborhood avoiding the other points of the divisor&amp;#39;s support. Provide public computation equations for both directions. The local sphere-map facts live with `sphereMap`, and the existing bundled finite-part specialization reuses the new local equation. No Mathlib infrastructure or external formalization is vendored. The new module cites Forster, Lectures on Riemann Surfaces, §16.

Add `TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/RiemannSurface/Divisor/Trivialization.lean` (400 lines) and update the existing `Meromorphic`, `SphereMap` and `FunctionField` support modules. Read the shared protocol and all ten rubrics: scope, correctness, reuse, attribution, api-design, generality, placement, naming, documentation and proof-quality. Check open and recently merged PR descriptions and search pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti before implementation and during self-review. Self-review generalizes local finite-order nonvanishing to normed complex vector spaces, delegates the existing bundled finite-part proof to the new local lemma, keeps generic image-open bookkeeping local to the construction, and verifies both exported coordinate equations from an importing-only module.

An importing-only modern client checks arbitrary normed complex vector targets without completeness, local existence, positive and negative point divisors, both categorical inverse laws, restriction naturality, and the removable value at the center. The inverse sends constant one to normalized `1/z` for `[0]` and to `z` for `-[0]`; the forward map recovers one at the center despite the unfilled pointwise product being zero there.

Synchronous local verification passes: both caches, plain whole-library `lake build --iofail` (68,716 jobs), the importing client, source style, the changed-module axiom audit and all 14 changed-module environment linters. The four changed files contain 478 insertions and 2 deletions. These are local checks, not CI; CI verifies the pushed head, including transitive axioms and global ownership checks.

`scope: scoped against 29bc6871728983707bc42137a8a1cd941b898bd7 (module list /home/mm/TauCetiWorker/checkouts/default/TauCeti/.lake/tauceti-scope/modules.txt)`

`local-axioms: checked 4 changed module(s), 280 declaration(s); 0 violation(s). Transitive axiom and global ownership checks run in CI.`

