  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/ee5a945da29044c5802562670d3bff07d5ca5e53</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/commit/ee5a945da29044c5802562670d3bff07d5ca5e53"/>
    <title>
        refactor(Algebra/Homology/AInfinity/Module/Right/Components): name th…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298123923?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>tauceti-redteam</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/tauceti-redteam</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(Algebra/Homology/AInfinity/Module/Right/Components): name the unsuspended module Stasheff expression (#29585)

Roadmap: DGAInfinity
&amp;lt;!--redteam:v1 {&amp;quot;owner&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;AI-DOOM-b743906b-281a-4ba5-939c-d5913cc9d39b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;findings&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;RT-20261105-cc0d05&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;patterns&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;repeated-reasoning&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;severity&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MINOR&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

## What was wrong

- **RT-20261105-cc0d05** (MINOR, confirmed): in `TauCeti/Algebra/Homology/AInfinity/Module/Right/Components.lean` the unsuspended module Stasheff expression, a 9-line double sum with its sign exponents, was written out in full four times: the right-hand side of `suspendedStasheff_eq_smul`, the statement of the public `stasheff`, and the hypothesis `hSI` of `apply_comp_gradedCoderiv_eq_zero` and of the public constructor `ofStasheff` (36 lines of one term, two of them in public statements). The algebra side of the library already names the corresponding expression: `TauCeti.AInfinity.stasheffSum` with `stasheffSum_def`, and `AInfinityAlgebra.stasheff` / `ofStasheff` are stated through it.

## Evidence

```
grep -n &amp;#39;negOnePowCast R (((k : ℤ) + 1) * ((n : ℤ) - k))&amp;#39; TauCeti/Algebra/Homology/AInfinity/Module/Right/Components.lean
# L514, L543, L647, L685 on origin/main: each the head of the same 9-line sum
```

**Decision (Fable definition agent):** add the def. It enters two public statements, but it mirrors the algebra-side API exactly (`stasheffSum`, `stasheffSum_def`), no file outside this one uses the module `stasheff` or `ofStasheff`, and the constructor interface becomes readable. Astra review is pending.

## The fix

New `def TauCeti.AInfinityRightModule.stasheffSum (AA) (m) (x : M) (e : ℤ) (d : ℕ → ℤ) (a : ℕ → A) (n : ℕ) : M`, the former expression verbatim, with the `rfl` unfolding lemma `stasheffSum_def` and the congruence lemma `stasheffSum_congr` (only `d i`, `a i` for `i &amp;lt; n` matter, as on the algebra side), placed just before `suspendedStasheff_eq_smul`. The four copies become `stasheffSum AA m x e d a n` (resp. `AA MM.m`); `suspendedStasheff_eq_smul` opens with `rw [stasheffSum_def]` and its proof is otherwise unchanged, and the other three proofs are untouched. The sign-convention paragraph moves from the docstring of `stasheff` to the def, and the module header lists the def. No declaration is renamed or deleted.

**Checks:** built `TauCeti.Algebra.Homology.AInfinity.Module.Right.Components` and its three importers `….Bimodule.Taylor`, `….Module.Right.Cohomology`, `….Module.Right.Hom.Components` with zero errors and zero warnings; `scripts/lint-style.sh` clean. Open PRs touching the file (open-PR file cache of 2026-11-06T06:07:30Z, 1708 open PRs): none.

## Why the changed definition is still the standard one

`stasheffSum` is literally the expression that was there (`stasheffSum_def` is `rfl`), so `stasheff` and `ofStasheff` state the same module Stasheff equations `∑ ± m(m(x, …), …) + ∑ ± m(x, …, m_A(…), …) = 0` as before, now in the shape the algebra side uses. Astra review is pending.

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

