    <title>
        refactor(Topology/Algebra/RestrictedProduct/Sum): split restricted pr…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T22:42:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6145801?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>harahu</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/harahu</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(Topology/Algebra/RestrictedProduct/Sum): split restricted products over a sum for MulMemClass reference sets (#29657)

Review pass over `TauCeti/Topology/Algebra/RestrictedProduct/Sum.lean`.

**Generalize.** The splitting `restrictedProductSum` of a restricted product over `ι₁ ⊕ ι₂`, and every lemma about it, assumed `[∀ k, Group (G k)]` and reference families `U : ∀ k, Subgroup (G k)`. None of this uses inverses or a unit. The file now takes Mathlib&amp;#39;s restricted-product idiom: `[∀ k, Mul (G k)]` with a subobject family `U : ∀ k, S k` where `[∀ k, SetLike (S k) (G k)] [∀ k, MulMemClass (S k) (G k)]`. That is exactly what the `Mul` instance on `Πʳ` needs, and it is the natural level for a `MulEquiv`. The splitting and its continuity results now also cover submonoid reference families, for example `𝒪_v` inside `K_v` as multiplicative monoids. The forward map is built from `RestrictedProduct.mapAlong` with `id` rather than `mapAlongMonoidHom` with `MonoidHom.id`, since the latter needs `Monoid`. It is the same function, and `map_mul&amp;#39;` is still `ext &amp;lt;;&amp;gt; rfl`.

**Documentation.**
- Docstrings now say &amp;quot;reference subsets&amp;quot; instead of &amp;quot;reference subgroups&amp;quot;, and the module docstring explains the `MulMemClass` level.
- The module docstring said &amp;quot;Everything here except that counterexample is also stated for additive groups&amp;quot;, but the counterexample `not_continuous_restrictedProductSum_symm` is not in this file. It is in `NotContinuousMul.lean`. The docstring now names that module and states that everything in this file has an additive version.

**Golf.** `hempty : cofinite ≤ 𝓟 ∅` over a finite type is now `by simp`.

**Callers.** No source changes were needed. `Away/Decomposition.lean` (subgroup families) and `NotContinuousMul.lean` (`fun _ ↦ ⊥`) elaborate unchanged against the generalized signature. Both modules, the only transitive importers of `Sum`, build.

Roadmap: RestrictedProducts

