    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;refactor(Analysis/InnerProductSpace/Harmonic/MeanValue/Basic): split the long sphere-Laplacian test-function proof into helpers (#28870)

Roadmap: none
&amp;lt;!--redteam:v1 {&amp;quot;owner&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;AI-DOOM-b743906b-281a-4ba5-939c-d5913cc9d39b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;findings&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;RT-20261105-faebb2&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;patterns&amp;quot;:[&amp;quot;long-proof&amp;quot;],&amp;quot;severity&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;MAJOR&amp;quot;}--&amp;gt;

## What was wrong
The private lemma `exists_integral_smul_laplacian_eq_two_smul_integral_deriv_smul` in `Harmonic/MeanValue/Basic.lean` had a 121-code-line proof, mixing three unrelated general constructions (shrinking a test-function support, smoothness of `psi (sqrt t) / (sqrt t)^n`, the radial weight identity and the sigma/rho primitive construction).

## Evidence
`awk` count of code lines of the proof on main be6518de91: 121. Statement unchanged (proof-only; no definition touched).

## The fix
Four helper lemmas, all public and each in a lower-level module: `TauCeti.exists_lt_tsupport_subset_Ioo` (new `Topology/Instances/Real/TSupport.lean`), `Real.contDiff_div_sqrt_pow` (`Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Sqrt.lean`, generalised from `C^∞` to `C^k`), and `TauCeti.pow_mul_add_eq_two_mul_deriv` and `TauCeti.exists_contDiff_eq_pow_mul_deriv` (new `Analysis/Calculus/RadialPrimitive.lean`); plus small golfs (`ContDiff.continuous_laplacian`, `tsupport_deriv_subset`). Main proof now 48 code lines. No name in the repo clashed (grep). Built the four touched modules and their direct importers with zero warnings; lint-style clean.

